00:02:50.500 --> 00:02:52.630
So the first thing,
BigQuery has now

00:02:52.630 --> 00:02:55.340
had beta support for a
query in Parquet and ROC

00:02:55.340 --> 00:02:57.740
file formats in cloud storage.

00:02:57.740 --> 00:02:59.628
And these new features
allow you to build

00:02:59.628 --> 00:03:01.420
a bridge between your
datasets and help you

00:03:01.420 --> 00:03:02.870
be a little bit more flexible.

00:03:02.870 --> 00:03:05.410
So your data stays in your
preferred open source formats

00:03:05.410 --> 00:03:10.600
in cloud storage and you can
use BigQuery's standard SQL

00:03:10.600 --> 00:03:12.350
for analytics and
data processing.

00:03:12.350 --> 00:03:13.770
So check the blog post out.

00:03:13.770 --> 00:03:16.450
I don't want to ruin too much,
but it's quite interesting.

00:03:16.450 --> 00:03:17.290
Parquet.

00:03:17.290 --> 00:03:18.040
SPEAKER 1: Butter.

00:03:18.040 --> 00:03:19.000
JON FOUST: [LAUGHS]

00:03:19.000 --> 00:03:20.500
MARK MIRCHANDANI:
Yeah, I think it's

00:03:20.500 --> 00:03:23.560
a great way for people to
have more ways to use BigQuery

00:03:23.560 --> 00:03:26.220
without needing to go through
some sort ETL process,

00:03:26.220 --> 00:03:28.810
or without having to
change their files.

00:03:28.810 --> 00:03:30.610
The more ways you can
ingest and then query

00:03:30.610 --> 00:03:33.080
